(A loop body is not a scope of its own (LANGUAGE.md: no block scoping),
 so a name declared inside one is available after the loop and the read
 below is in order. Bug #79's fix must not reject it: a loop body's
 declaration is never in the whole-program "definite" set - the loop may
 run zero times - so this read is answered by the walk alone.)

Repeat 2 times, a number called tally is 5.
Print tally.

Repeat 0 times, a number called untouched is 42.
Print untouched.
